/* 帛画 · 帛画乘风飞来，铺平在墙上 (v5, the owner's idea) — the passage from the 虎食人卣 (jijin) into the 人物御龙帛画.
   One discovery: a gust from the left carries the painting itself — silk and bamboo rod — into the hall, sweeps it past the bronze,
   and hangs it on the wall; the wind dies, the swinging and rippling die down, the silk lies flat — and in it the man's hat ribbons
   and the canopy tassels still stream back, the way the real wind blew: the wind stayed in the painting.
   Beats (seconds of D = 13.2, see T):
   ① 0–0.9    the 卣 at rest.
   ② 0.9–3.5  the painting on its rod blows in from the left, near the camera, billowing, and sweeps across the bronze
              (the bronze is gone behind it); the rod swings on past and back to its place on the wall.
   ③ 3.5–7.9  it hangs from the rod and swings/ripples in the dying wind; big waves → small ripples → still, perfectly flat.
   ④ 7.9–13.2 THE MOMENT: the wind has stopped, everything is still and stays still (no lean-in: the owner asked for none) —
              the canopy tassels and the hat ribbons still stream back; title 11.4, label 12.2; p 1 = wall + the painting + its soft drop shadow.
   fix-bohua-1: the video is only ever drawn whole (drawImage(v,0,0) into FR each frame), its parts are cut from FR — some Chrome
   builds draw a video's sub-rectangle wrongly (the owner's: the T part came out black → black wall with a wall-coloured column);
   the mp4 is tagged sRGB/BT.709/limited (was 'unknown' transfer: Chrome converted it as BT.709 video and the silk came out ~10 levels
   brighter than the page's own pixels → a jump at the hand-over); the cross-fade to the page's pixels is 7.9–8.6 (≥ 0.5 s).
   The cloth is an offline cloth simulation (PBD, _wip/t-bohua/v5/sim.py; top row pinned to the kinematic rod, wind that dies,
   damping) rendered in Blender EEVEE with the painting's own scan as the silk texture and the rod's own scan on a cylinder
   (render.py; lit so that the flat silk renders as its texture), stored as rooms/bohua/t_cloth.mp4: rows 0–1615 = premultiplied colour
   E (2160×1616), rows 1632–2439 × cols 0–1079 = transmittance T = (1 − α)·wall shadow at half resolution; composited here as
   dst·T (multiply) + E (lighter). The last simulated frames are exactly flat; the video then cross-fades to the hung work's own pixels.
   Rest: the soft drop shadow round the silk (on #fx, above the hung work, so the silk is knocked out of it) — EH_SHARED.bohuaRest. */
