/* 兰亭 · 鼓槌一挥，成了笔（入部：人与佛）— the passage from the Eastern Han drummer-storyteller (shuochang) into the
   Shenlong copy of the 兰亭序 (lanting). v1.
   One discovery: the drumstick the storyteller holds up is swung — the camera rides the arc of its tip (pivot = the fist), the tomb
   smears away in the swing's motion blur and is swept open behind it onto the new room, and the arc comes to rest exactly where
   王羲之's brush starts the first dot of 永; the writing runs on in the swing's momentum. The Han hand that beat a drum becomes the
   Jin hand that writes its own mind.
   Beats (seconds of D = 14, see T):
   ① 0–1.0    the drummer at rest (p 0 = shuochang rest: wall #1B1411 + cut-out + EH_SHARED.shuochangRest floor shadow).
   ② 1.0–3.34 the camera pushes in on the raised drumstick (rigid scale/translate of the photograph, never past 1:1 — the
              original-resolution cut t_fig_hi.webp takes over above main_cut's 1:1), stops, and draws back 14 px (蓄势).
   ③ 3.34–3.86 the swing: the camera follows the stick's tip along its 88° arc (1/30 s motion blur, up to 12 samples, mip-biased);
              3.39–3.69 a soft front sweeps the dark away behind the swing onto the new room; the scroll arrives from the lower
              left, braking, and stops with 永's first dot where the arc ends.
   ④ 3.86–9.65 **THE MOMENT: from that dot 永和九年歲在癸丑暮春之初會 is written stroke by stroke in the original's own ink
              (the photograph's ink pixels, revealed in their arrival order), slow at first and faster and faster; 人与佛 settles
              on the wall to the right (part name, full 6.25–8.95).**
   ⑤ 8.7–14   the other 27 columns follow right → left ever faster while the camera pulls back to the hung scroll (9.4–13.2);
              13.1–13.6 the WebGL picture hands over to the DOM-identical copy of main.webp; p 1 = wall #3E443C + main.webp.
   Rendering: WebGL2, one full-screen shader drawn onto the stage: tomb (t_fig_hi) + lanting (cut/paper_hd, cut/ink_hd,
   t_time.png = per-pixel arrival time, 16 bit in R/G, dilated) + the sweep front + motion-blur samples. No per-pixel JS, no
   canvases created while playing, no ctx.filter. Without WebGL2 the scroll arrives whole (no stroke order).
   Offline: _wip/t-lanting/timemap.py (writing schedule → t_time.png), fighi.py (hi-res cut from the prep matte).
   Rest: nothing is painted over the hung scroll — EH_SHARED.lantingRest is a no-op for the next room. */
