/* 蛙声 · 立轴垂落，蛙声由远而近 — the passage from the 洋彩玲珑转旋瓶 (yangcai) into 齐白石《蛙声十里出山泉》, the last room.
   One discovery (plan_b5 蛙声): a narrow hanging scroll is let down in front of us and the camera rides down with its roller —
   distant peaks, two walls of ink rock, a white mountain stream; the frogs are heard nearer and nearer; at the bottom only a few
   tadpoles come out of the roll with the water, and there is not one frog anywhere: the frogs are in the viewer's ear.
   Physical logic: one object, a real hanging scroll. It is lowered rolled up, hangs from its top rod, and the roll (with the
   roller inside it) drops at an even pace, unrolling the sheet above it; the roll gets thinner as it pays out (its cross-section
   shrinks with the paper left on it, r² ∝ length) until only the bare roller is left — exactly the roller theme.css draws at rest.
   The painting never moves on its sheet and is never stretched: the roll's centre line is the lower edge of what is shown.
   Beats (seconds of D = 13.8, see T):
   ① 0–1.2     the vase at rest (p 0 = yangcai rest: wall + wash + the cut vase + EH_SHARED.yangcaiRest).
   ② 1.2–3.4   the camera draws back: the vase gets smaller (whole-scene zoom about the screen centre), the palace wall turns into the
               pale wall of this room (1.5–3.3); the vase fades out while small (2.8–3.3).
   ③ 3.3–4.3   the scroll, rolled up, is lowered into the top of the frame and hangs (ease-out, ≈ 125 px).
   ④ 4.3–10.6  **the moment: the roll drops at an even ≈ 300 px/s, the sheet unrolls above it — mounting, distant peaks, rock walls,
               the white stream, the tadpoles one after another coming out of the roll; the camera (0.4 CSS px per source px, ≤ 1:1 at
               dpr 2) takes up the roll once it is ¾ down the screen and rides down with it; at the bottom the roll stops short
               (0.35 s) — that is where the frog chorus, at its loudest, stops dead (sound: audio/cues/washeng.json).**
   ⑤ 10.6–11.2 stillness on the bottom of the stream.   11.2–13.6 the camera draws back to the whole scroll on the wall = p 1.
   Rendering: plain 2D. The sheet of the mount (theme.css .frame.f-mount ::before, painted as the CSS draws it) is rendered once at the
   moment scale; the painting is drawn from an ImageBitmap of main.webp with a source crop (no scaling above 1:1); the shadows are
   pre-rendered 3-slice sprites; the roll is two cached unit gradients. Everything is built in init / warm-up during the vase's rest.
   Rest: the hung painting in its mount (the DOM's) — EH_SHARED.washengRest is a no-op. */
