/* Special exhibit "balance_scroll" (八大 · 一点定一张纸).
   A blank hanging scroll on one nail. Its cord is knotted off-centre, so the empty sheet hangs crooked. Press and hold on the paper to put
   down ink: the longer the press, the larger and heavier the blot (area grows with time, 洇 halo soaks out after release); ink cannot be taken
   back. The scroll is a rigid body on a single pivot (paper + silk mount + top rod + heavy bottom rod + every blot as a point mass):
   θ'' = g·Σm(x cosθ − y sinθ)/I − 2ζω₀θ', so it swings, overshoots and settles at tanθ = Σmx / Σmy. Ink far from the cord's line weighs
   more (lever); ink on the heavy side makes it worse. When the equilibrium is within ±0.3° and it has come to rest, the cord "catches":
   the scroll snaps still (定), one 箫 note, and the panel tells how much ink it took against the least this sheet needs. Drag the bottom rod
   (or the mount) to swing it by hand; it creaks at each turn. Three sheets with different knots/proportions; nothing of 八大's own shapes.
   Text: room.special.{title,text,hints.*,captions.*,sheets,colors}. Sound: recorded bad-* (audio/parts/sfx-bada.json) by name, else the
   engine's synth voices / EH.audio bus; never an own AudioContext.
   Keys (taken at the window while open, whatever has focus except buttons/fields): W A S D move the brush, hold Enter to ink, F nudge,
   R wash and start over, N next sheet. Space ← → Esc stay with the engine. */
