/* Special exhibit "bridge_mast" (汴京 · 虹桥下过船).
   The visitor is the crew of the big boat in the 虹桥 passage of 《清明上河图》. The current carries the boat toward the timber arch; its A-frame
   mast is far too tall for the arch, and the trackers' tow line is tied to the mast head. One pointer, two jobs, taken in turns:
   · drag DOWN (on the scene or on the control strip) = pay out the lowering rope. The mast is a heavy pole on a hinge: the lower it leans the
     harder gravity pulls it (torque ∝ sin tilt), so paying out fast near the end lets it fall free and slam onto the cabin roof (the boat jolts,
     the bow is knocked off line). Pay out slowly for the last part.
   · press and HOLD = plant the punt poles (撑篙) at the bow: the bow is pushed back in line and the boat slows. A stroke lasts ≈ 1.4 s, then the
     pole has run out: let go and plant again.
   Lowering the mast lets go of the tow (the line is tied to its head): while towed the boat runs straight; untowed, the current turns the bow
   (an unstable yaw, stronger near the piers). Lower too early → a long untowed drift, the boat swings broadside (打横) and hits the abutment;
   too late → the mast head strikes the arch (撞桥). People on the bridge lean over the rail and shout louder as the danger grows; clear the
   arch and the bridge cheers. Physics: ψ'' = −k·tow·ψ − cψ' + (1−tow)(λψ + gust) + pole; τ'' = G sin τ − cτ' − rope spring.
   Wide screens: the hung work is the whole scroll; while the exhibit is open everything but the 虹桥 passage is veiled with the wall colour and
   the passage is bracketed; the brackets pulse with the danger. Nothing is drawn on the passage itself.
   The scene below is a drawn model (ink line on silk); the river is the painting's own water lines (s_water.webp, from the 虹桥 passage);
   the real passage is shown under the model (s_hongqiao.webp). Text: room.special.{hints.*, labels.*, captions.*, bridge}.
   Sound: recorded bjg-* of this room (audio/parts/sfx-bianjing.json) looked up by name, else the engine's synth; never an own AudioContext.
   Keys (taken at the window while the exhibit is on screen; a focused button keeps its keys): hold ↓ or S = pay out, hold ↑ or W = pole,
   R = again. Space ← → Esc stay with the engine. */
