/* Special exhibit "ink_bleed_grapes" (写意 · 笔底明珠).
   A sheet of raw xuan paper in the reading panel and a brush that holds a real amount of water and ink.
   - Press and hold on the paper: the brush belly presses down and keeps feeding liquid; the ink creeps out along the paper fibres
     (a small water simulation on a 480×360 grid: water held per cell, passed on along fibres, pigment carried more slowly than water,
     evaporation, more pigment settling at the drying front). The longer you hold, the bigger and wetter the grape.
   - Press wet ink onto ink that is still half-dry: the new water pushes the old pigment outward and leaves a dark water line (破墨).
     On ink that has already dried it only darkens, no water line.
   - Drag and flick: a vine stroke made of bristles that each run dry on their own; the faster you go the more paper shows through (飞白),
     and on release the brush keeps travelling for a moment as it lifts, so a fast flick ends in a dry, tapering tail (and may throw drops).
   - 笔里的水 少 / 中 / 多: every time the brush goes down it is loaded at that level – little water = dark ink that spreads slowly,
     much water = pale ink that runs far (墨分五色).
   - 对照原作: the sheet turns into a detail of Xu Wei's scroll (crops from the full-resolution scan, s_cmp_*.webp) and a ring marks the
     same place on the hung scroll. After each mark a small detail of the matching place is offered.
   The visitor's sheet is never hung: the scroll on the wall stays as it is.
   Text: room.special.labels / hints / captions / compare[{label, box:[x,y,w,h] in main.webp px}]; fallbacks below.
   Sounds: the room's recorded sfx xyi-press (loop) xyi-flick xyi-drop xyi-paper xyi-water, else engine synth.
   Keys (captured at the window while open): hold F = press the brush; while F is held ↑ ↓ / W A S D drag it; K = a flick;
   1 2 3 = water; C = a new sheet. */
