/* Special exhibit "lasso_pole" (百骏 · 套马).
   A meadow seen from where you stand, a hard side light (its direction from cut/layers.json light.shadow_vec, measured in the scroll: shadows fall left), and one horse after another
   cantering past with its shadow running beside it. You hold a long 套马杆 (its butt is in your hands, below the frame).
   Press and hold (aim with the pointer: the ring on the grass is where the loop will come down), let go: the pole is raised and bent back
   while you hold (the longer the hold, the farther it can throw, up to ~0.55 s), then whips forward; the rope loop leaves the tip on a
   parabola. The loop has to come down over the horse's head as it gets there: lands ahead → early, behind → late, aside → wide; a loop
   that falls near the horse spooks it (neigh, it swerves and gallops). Caught: the rope snaps taut, the pole bends toward the horse and
   the horse drags you across the grass; press and hold to brace (the pole is pressed down, the horse slows and swings round you on the
   rope until it stands). Don't brace and the horse pulls free. The pole is an angle spring (inertia, overshoot = its spring); the bend
   shows lag, weight and tension. A button takes the shadows away (as in every painting before this room): the loop's height and the
   horse's distance become hard to read — the shadows are what make the 阴阳远近 (depth) legible. The horses are drawn the way Castiglione
   painted them (modelled light and dark, a cast shadow on the ground); the gallop follows Muybridge's photographs (1878), not a horse cut
   out of the scroll. Wide screens: a horse that pulls free gallops out of the panel along the floor below the hung scroll, with its shadow
   falling the same way, and is gone. 看画里的套马人 (also shown after the first catch): a detail of the scroll (room.special.scene boxes, hr tile)
   in the panel and, on wide screens, four quiet corner marks around that scene on the hung work; nothing else is drawn on the scroll.
   Text: room.special.{title,text,hints.*,captions.*,coats,shadow{dx,dy}}; cut/layers.json may give the painting's shadow direction
   (shadowDir [dx,dy] / light.shadowDir / shadow.dir, image px, y down).
   Sound: recorded bjn-* (sfx-baijun.json) looked up by name, else the engine's synth voices; never an own AudioContext.
   Keys (taken at the window while the exhibit is open; a focused button keeps its keys): W A S D / ↑ ↓ move the aim,
   hold Enter to raise the pole, let go to throw; after a catch hold Enter to brace. Space ← → Esc stay with the engine. */
