/* Special exhibit "oil_lamp" (九色鹿 · 燃灯照壁).
   The visitor carries a small clay oil lamp through the dark cave: while the panel is open the hung band goes dark (the cave), and only the pool
   of light around the flame shows the wall. The lamp has weight (it follows the hand on a damped spring and overshoots a little); the flame is
   a damped oscillator driven by the lamp's velocity and acceleration: it trails and leans when you move, shrinks when you move fast and goes
   out (with a curl of smoke) if you keep rushing — stand still a moment and it catches again. The eye adapts: a spot the light rests on turns
   from dim grey (s_dim.webp) to full colour over ~2 s (a low-res adaptation grid), so the 石绿 and 土红 "come out" only where you linger.
   Distance: wheel / pinch / 拉远·凑近 moves the lamp away from the wall (bigger, softer, dimmer pool, and the 晕染 read as relief — four
   pre-rendered raking-light shadings s_rel_{l,r,u,d}.webp blended soft-light, each weighted by where the lamp is) or close to it (small bright
   pool, flat): 许嵩's "远望眼晕如凹凸，就视即平", borrowed. Nine scenes (room.special.scenes) count as seen once the light has rested on them;
   the story runs from both ends to the middle, and when the light first rests on the deer before the king the wick cracks ("噼") and flares.
   Wide screens: an overlay canvas on the hung work (api.artRect()); narrow screens: a stage in the panel that follows the lamp along the band.
   All visible text comes from room.special (hints, captions, scenes, labels); the defaults below are only fallbacks.
   Sound: recorded jsl-* sounds when the room's sound designer ships them (see REC), else the engine's synth voices / EH.audio.out(). */
