/* Special exhibit "polo" (三彩 · 击鞠).
   A Tang polo field seen from the stands (oblique), one rider on a horse dressed like the hung 三彩马 (amber body, cream mane, legs and
   upturned tail, green rosettes on dark straps, pale saddle cloth). Press and hold on the field: the horse gallops and turns toward the
   pointer. It has weight: speed builds and bleeds off slowly, the turn rate is limited by grip (a_lat / v), so at a full gallop it cannot
   make a tight turn and slides wide (dust); slow down to turn. Let go to swing the crescent stick (月杖): the moment the stick comes down
   decides the shot: ball right at the stick head → a clean hit, ball still ahead → an air swing (early), ball already past → it rolls by
   the hooves (late). Where along the stick head the ball was sets the direction, the horse's speed sets the distance (and how high it
   flies). Through the goal at the right end: a drum. One round = 60 s, then the horse stands still and is shown beside the hung horse.
   Wide screens (the hung work visible beside the panel): a hard, high shot that clears the field's low wall flies out of the panel and
   lands on the floor in front of the hung horse, rolls up against its base and stops (a soft knock). Catch it and throw it back onto the
   field, or leave it: it flies home after a while. Nothing is drawn over the horse itself.
   Text: room.special.{title,text,hints.*,captions.*,colors,cutBox,points.floorY}; geometry: cut/layers.json (floorY, base polygon).
   Sound: recorded san-* (sfx-sancai.json) looked up by name, else the engine's synth voices; never an own AudioContext.
   Keys (canvas focused): ↑ or W hold to gallop, A / D steer, let go of ↑ (or Enter) to swing. Space ← → Esc stay with the engine. */
