/* Special exhibit "rotating_core" (洋彩 · 转心).
   The 洋彩玲珑转旋瓶 (台北故宫) is four pieces: neck, pierced outer belly, inner vase, base. The neck is locked to the inner vase, so turning
   the neck turns the inner vase behind the fixed openwork (museum description). The visitor is the hand on the neck: drag sideways on the
   hung vase, on the close-up in the panel or on the "瓶颈" grip, or hold A / D, and the inner vase turns with weight: static friction to
   break (porcelain on porcelain), inertia after a flick, Coulomb + viscous drag, a little tap when it comes to rest. Hold S (or press and
   hold on the vase) to brake. Through the holes the clouds and red bats of the inner vase (云蝠纹) drift past; spun fast they blur into
   a running-horse lantern; stop a red bat right between the two dragons and the caption says so.
   Data (rooms/yangcai, made by _wip/s-rotating_core/prep.py): s_core.webp = the inner vase unrolled from three museum photos (PAO, PAE,
   PAG) of the inner vase alone, about 120° each, seams blended (schematic at the seams); s_holes.webp = alpha mask of the openwork in the
   pierced band (thresholded from the hung photo); s_geo.json = geometry in the original photo's pixels (2291 × 3055).
   The hung work stays as it is until the visitor first turns the neck; only the holes are painted over, nothing else of the vase.
   Texts: room.special.{hint, hintTouch, hintWall, hintWallTouch, keys, note, captions{bat, cloud, fast, idle}, labels{neck, left, right, turns}}. */
